      "writtenOn": "2015-04-17T23:52:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m confused by \n\n   gpionum/10\n\nand\n\n   (1\u003c\u003c(gpionum%10))\n\nAren\u0027t those MEC1322-specific?  Some other EC may group the GPIOs differently.  And isn\u0027t each pinbase really a port?  (That is, each group of 10 interrupts shares a set of registers/interrupt/etc?)\n\nI think this is a worthwhile change overall, but I think we need to figure out how to make it more general.\n\nPerhaps if the chip config does something like\n\n  #define CONFIG_GPIO_PER_REG 10\n\nor\n\n  #define CONFIG_GPIO_GROUP_SIZE 10\n\n(open to suggestions on the name)\n\nand then this code can use that value to calculate the port and mask values instead of hard-coding 10.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "7f11ff945ef9ca94e1a6586e326f3529780199ff",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
